# 3. CUSTOMER-APPROVED BUSINESS WORKFLOW

The final frontend must reflect these approved business rules.

## Individual Student 5-Good

Student prepares application
→ Student submits
→ School preliminary review
→ School consolidates recommended applications
→ School attaches one official decision document
→ School forwards one batch
→ City receives applications
→ Authorized City reviewers assess directly
→ Committee records official decisions.

## University of Da Nang

Eight original member institutions:

- DUT.
- DUE.
- UED.
- UFL.
- UTE.
- VKU.
- VNUK.
- SMP.

Share:

`unit-udn`

The School reviewer uses one consolidated unit-wide list.

One forwarding batch per season.

One common official decision document.

One successful final forwarding.

Original student institution identities remain distinct.

## City review

No mandatory individual City Officer assignment.

No workload allocation subsystem.

No separate ambiguous-case Resolution Hub.

Authorized City reviewers use the shared review workspace.

## Committee

Internal review by authorized accounts.

No fictional meetings, hearings, officer questioning, voting/quorum procedures or generated meeting minutes.

Committee official decisions remain human-controlled.

## Collective

Collective applications use TT01–TT04 and proceed directly to City.

They must not enter the Individual School forwarding batch.

## AI

Optional, helpful and non-intrusive.

AI advisory assessments never create official human decisions.

