# 20. REAL MODE VS DEMO MODE

Treat these as distinct execution modes.

## Demo Mode

Must provide a complete, coherent, interactive synthetic end-to-end scenario.

Requirements:

- Correct fixture identities.
- Consistent application statuses.
- Working review actions.
- Working batch forwarding simulation.
- Working Committee decision simulation.
- Coherent Dashboard totals.
- Valid Demo exports.
- Deterministic reset.
- No fake live-data claims.

## Real Mode

Must use actual authorized backend contracts.

Requirements:

- No synthetic fallback.
- No fabricated successful API responses.
- Correct authorization.
- Actual server-confirmed mutation states.
- Honest network/database errors.
- No localStorage pretending to be durable production persistence.

When PostgreSQL is offline, do not claim full Real Mode integration testing has passed.

